    "section": "disclosures",
    "title": "Aramco closes acquisition of 22.5% of Petro Rabigh",
    "title_en": null,
    "impact": null,
    "summary": "Saudi Aramco announced the completion of its acquisition of 375.97 million Class A ordinary shares in Petro Rabigh, representing about 22.5% of its capital, from Japan’s Sumitomo Chemical. Aramco financed the transaction from its own cash, increasing its ownership of Class A shares to approximately 60%. A payment of SAR 2.63 billion (SAR 7 per share) was made for the acquisition. The deal aims to strengthen Petro Rabigh's financial position and support its long-term strategy through joint investment by Aramco and Sumitomo."
   },
   {
    "date": "2025-09-17T21:00:00",
